          "line": 1,
          "text": "# HCN GIAO shielding plan"
        },
        {
          "line": 2,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 3,
          "text": "Requested system: neutral, singlet HCN in the gas phase, atoms ordered H-C-N."
        },
        {
          "line": 4,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 5,
          "text": "Method choice: PBE0 (RKS for the closed-shell singlet). PBE0 is an allowed one-parameter hybrid functional (25% HF exchange) and is inexpensive for three atoms while including exact-exchange admixture relevant to shielding. Basis choice: def2-TZVP, an allowed polarized valence triple-zeta basis; the larger flexible basis is preferable to def2-SVP for anisotropic GIAO tensors while remaining modest for HCN under the four-core / 192 MB-per-process limits."
        },
        {
          "line": 6,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
          "line": 7,
          "text": "Planned ORCA controls: gas phase (no solvent), charge 0, multiplicity 1, RKS, PBE0/def2-TZVP, GIAO NMR shielding for all nuclei. Resource settings will be recorded in the actual input as required by the native input contract."
        },
        {
          "line": 8,
          "text": ""
        },
        {
